{
  "id": "3d88595d9d4c80fbbd97df2f625f35d1",
  "title": "Even and Odd- testing",
  "source": { "type": "notion-export", "ref": "https://app.notion.com/p/3d88595d9d4c80fbbd97df2f625f35d1" },
  "blocks": [
    { "id": "intro", "type": "heading-2", "text": "Introduction" },
    { "id": "definition", "type": "heading-3", "text": "Definition" },
    { "id": "definition-text", "type": "paragraph", "text": "An integer is **even** if it can be divided into two equal integer groups. If it cannot, it is **odd**. This includes **zero** and **negative integers** too." },
    { "id": "definition-divider", "type": "divider" },
    { "id": "representing", "type": "heading-3", "text": "Representing Even and Odd numbers" },
    { "id": "even", "type": "heading-4", "text": "Even integers" },
    { "id": "even-text", "type": "paragraph", "text": "If x is even, then it can be written as:" },
    { "id": "even-equation", "type": "equation", "text": "x = 2a, a ∈ ℤ" },
    { "id": "even-odd-divider", "type": "divider" },
    { "id": "odd", "type": "heading-4", "text": "Odd integers" },
    { "id": "odd-text", "type": "paragraph", "text": "When integers are paired in groups of two, an odd integer always leaves **one** behind.\n\nAn integer *y* is **odd** if it can be written as:" },
    { "id": "odd-equation", "type": "equation", "text": "y = 2b + 1, b ∈ ℤ" },
    { "id": "integer-callout", "type": "callout", "text": "We use ℤ—the set of all integers—because even and odd numbers include positive integers, zero, and negative integers.", "metadata": { "icon": "💡" } },
    { "id": "think", "type": "heading-4", "text": "Think Like a Mathematician" },
    { "id": "think-prompt", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Try to answer yourself before looking at the logic" },
    { "id": "toggle-3", "type": "toggle", "text": "Why not write an odd number as 2b + 3?", "children": [{ "type": "equation", "text": "2b + 3 = 2(b+1) + 1" }, { "type": "paragraph", "text": "Since b+1 is also an integer, this is still the same basic odd form." }] },
    { "id": "toggle-2", "type": "toggle", "text": "Why is 2b + 2 even?", "children": [{ "type": "equation", "text": "2b + 2 = 2(b+1)" }, { "type": "paragraph", "text": "It is a multiple of 2, so it is even." }] },
    { "id": "assumption", "type": "callout", "text": "**Useful assumption**\nIf x is even and y is odd, we can write:", "metadata": { "icon": "💡" }, "children": [{ "type": "equation", "text": "x = 2a    and    y = 2b + 1" }, { "type": "paragraph", "text": "for some integers a and b." }] },
    { "id": "try-first", "type": "heading-2", "text": "Try it yourself" },
    { "id": "try-placeholder", "type": "paragraph", "text": "[questions to be added here]", "metadata": { "placeholder": true } },
    { "id": "application", "type": "heading-2", "text": "Application" },
    { "id": "addition", "type": "heading-3", "text": "Addition and subtraction activity" },
    { "id": "addition-prompt", "type": "paragraph", "text": "Try each question before opening the answer." },
    { "id": "addition-question", "type": "paragraph", "text": "What is the sum of:" },
    { "id": "add-even", "type": "toggle", "text": "Two even integers → odd or even?", "children": [{ "type": "paragraph", "text": "**Answer: Even**" }, { "type": "equation", "text": "2a + 2b = 2(a+b)" }] },
    { "id": "add-odd", "type": "toggle", "text": "Two odd integers → odd or even?", "children": [{ "type": "paragraph", "text": "**Answer: Even**" }, { "type": "equation", "text": "(2a+1) + (2b+1) = 2(a+b+1)" }] },
    { "id": "add-mixed", "type": "toggle", "text": "One even and one odd integer → odd or even?", "children": [{ "type": "paragraph", "text": "**Answer: Odd**" }, { "type": "equation", "text": "2a + (2b+1) = 2(a+b)+1" }] },
    { "id": "subtraction", "type": "callout", "text": "The same parity rules apply to subtraction:\neven − even = even;\nodd − odd = even;\neven − odd = odd.", "metadata": { "icon": "💡" } },
    { "id": "multiplication", "type": "heading-3", "text": "Multiplication activity" },
    { "id": "mult-even", "type": "toggle", "text": "Two even integers → odd or even?", "children": [{ "type": "paragraph", "text": "**Answer: Even**" }, { "type": "equation", "text": "(2a)(2b) = 2(2ab)" }] },
    { "id": "mult-odd", "type": "toggle", "text": "Two odd integers → odd or even?", "children": [{ "type": "paragraph", "text": "**Answer: Odd**" }, { "type": "equation", "text": "(2a+1)(2b+1) = 2(2ab+a+b)+1" }] },
    { "id": "mult-mixed", "type": "toggle", "text": "One even and one odd integer → odd or even?", "children": [{ "type": "paragraph", "text": "**Answer: Even**" }, { "type": "equation", "text": "(2a)(2b+1) = 2(a(2b+1))" }, { "type": "paragraph", "text": "The factor 2 makes the product even." }] },
    { "id": "challenge", "type": "heading-2", "text": "Try it yourself" },
    { "id": "challenge-prompt", "type": "callout", "text": "Determine whether y is odd or even when:", "metadata": { "icon": "💡" }, "children": [{ "type": "equation", "text": "y = x² + 3x" }] },
    { "id": "challenge-solution", "type": "toggle", "text": "Show the solution", "children": [{ "type": "paragraph", "text": "If x is odd, x² and 3x are odd, so their sum is even. If x is even, x² and 3x are even, so their sum is even. Therefore y is always even." }] },
    { "id": "practice", "type": "heading-2", "text": "Practise" },
    { "id": "practice-placeholder", "type": "paragraph", "text": "[MCQs to be added here]", "metadata": { "placeholder": true } },
    { "id": "memory", "type": "heading-2", "text": "Memory check" },
    { "id": "memory-callout", "type": "callout", "text": "Key takeaway", "metadata": { "icon": "💡" }, "children": [{ "type": "bulleted-list", "children": [
      { "type": "paragraph", "text": "Even integers have the form 2a; odd integers have the form 2b+1, where a,b ∈ ℤ." },
      { "type": "paragraph", "text": "Same-parity addition or subtraction is even; mixed parity is odd." },
      { "type": "paragraph", "text": "A product is even if at least one factor is even." },
      { "type": "paragraph", "text": "0 is even, and negative numbers can be odd or even." }
    ] }] }
  ]
}
